abstract: >-
  Twelve self-contained, end-to-end machine learning use cases for the shipping and
  logistics industry: delivery-commitment risk, quantile ETAs, intervention
  optimization, network anomaly detection, volume forecasting, route optimization,
  dynamic pricing, predictive maintenance, address resolution, returns prediction,
  capacity planning, and exception triage. Each includes a synthetic generator with a
  documented ground-truth process, audited cleaning, honest operational baselines,
  evaluation in operational units, and explainability grounded by tests.
